# Git Commit Conventions

## Format

```
[TAG] Short description in imperative mood
```

## Tags

| Tag | When |
|-----|------|
| `[FEAT]` | New feature or significant functionality |
| `[FIX]` | Bug fix |
| `[REFACTOR]` | Code restructuring without behavior change |
| `[CONFIG]` | Build, Gradle, plugin, CI/CD, or config changes |
| `[DOCS]` | Documentation only |
| `[TEST]` | Adding or updating tests |
| `[STYLE]` | Formatting, whitespace, naming (no logic change) |

## Examples from This Project

```
[FEAT] Implement syncUserProfile and refresh on splash and settings
[FEAT] Wire email login/register UI to UserRepository
[FIX] Align protobuf with Firestore protolite-well-known-types
[CONFIG] Split Firebase convention plugin into app and library variants
[REFACTOR] Rename Auth screen and route to Login
```

## Rules

- Tag is uppercase in square brackets
- Description starts with imperative verb (Implement, Add, Fix, Wire, Create, Update, Remove)
- Keep under 72 characters
- No period at the end
- Reference feature area if helpful (e.g., "on dashboard and settings pages")
